# FlintTrade — screener

> Market scanner, OI analysis, PCR, max pain, futures quadrant, portfolio Greeks, GEX, IV analysis, vol surface

## Key Modules
- `option_chain.py` — Option chain data fetching and processing
- `oi_analysis.py` — Open interest analysis, PCR, OI spurts
- `oi_profile.py` — OI profile visualization data
- `greeks.py` — Portfolio Greeks calculation (Black-Scholes)
- `gex.py` — Gamma exposure analysis
- `iv_analysis.py` — Implied volatility analysis
- `iv_smile.py` — IV smile/skew visualization
- `vol_surface.py` — Volatility surface construction
- `straddle_pnl.py` — Straddle P&L analysis
- `futures_quadrant.py` — Futures OI vs price quadrant
- `scanner.py` — Market scanner with configurable filters
- `rrg.py` — Relative Rotation Graph
- `stock_cache.py` / `stock_routes.py` — Stock data caching and routes
- `analysis_routes.py` — Analysis API routes

## Dependencies

See `packages/services/screener/pyproject.toml` for declared dependencies and optional extras.

## Additional pip libraries
- py_vollib_vectorized — vectorized Black-Scholes Greeks (use this over hand-rolled math)
- mibian — simple options pricing for quick calculations
- NSE-Option-Chain-Analyzer (VarunS2002) — reference for OI trend analysis patterns

## Feature scope clarification
- screener CALCULATES: Greeks, PCR, max pain, OI analysis, support/resistance from OI
- terminal DISPLAYS the results from screener
- dashboard shows portfolio-level Greeks summary from screener

## Crypto screening
- BTC/ETH options Greeks via Delta Exchange
- Funding rate arbitrage detection (perpetuals vs futures)
- Cross-exchange price comparison (optional — `pip install ccxt` if needed)

## Free data sources (no broker API needed)
- nsepython — NSE option chain, FII/DII data, PCR, advance/decline
- openchart — Free NSE/NFO historical data
- yfinance — Global data and international commodity futures proxies; INR conversion is approximate and does not provide native MCX exchange prices.
